<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Ravenna</h1><p class="st-meta">1275 CE – 1441 CE · capital Ravenna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The da Polenta lordship over the old imperial city of Ravenna, which sheltered Dante in his last years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1275 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guido-i-da-polenta">Guido da Polenta</a>, called the Elder, took control of Ravenna, ancient capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a> and the Byzantine exarchate. His family ruled as lords and later as papal vicars within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-polenta-family">da Polenta</a> ruled a city whose glory lay in the past, living from the farmland and salt pans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> coast. Guido's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesca-da-rimini">Francesca</a> married into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatesta-family">Malatesta of Rimini</a> and became the tragic heroine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inferno-dante">Dante's Inferno</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guido-novello-da-polenta">Guido Novello da Polenta</a> welcomed the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, who died in Ravenna in 1321 and is buried there. Later members of the family were often violent, and they grew dependent on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1441 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> expelled the last lord, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostasio-iii-da-polenta">Ostasio III da Polenta</a>, and annexed Ravenna to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a>. After 1509 the city returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1275 CE – 1441 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.07%;width:3.30%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1275 CE – 1441 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ravenna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Guido I da Polenta, Guido Novello da Polenta, Ostasio III da Polenta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romagnol, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Da Polenta lordship, Ravenna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1358&amp;focus=lordship-of-ravenna" aria-label="Lordship of Ravenna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4972 607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Ravenna lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5292 863L5304 942M5292 863L5293 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5293 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5292 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5292 863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ravenna. <a href="/atlas?year=1358&amp;focus=lordship-of-ravenna">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

